      "title": "[RFC] Consolidating and Modernizing Integration Test Architecture for gz_ros2_control",
      "link": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/rfc-consolidating-and-modernizing-integration-test-architecture-for-gz-ros2-control/58883",
      "summary": "Hi everyone, Over time, the integration test suite in gz_ros2_control has grown incrementally as new controllers, demos, and interfaces were introduced. While these tests prevent regressions, the lack of a explicit test architecture currently leads to duplicate simulation launches, unnecessary CI runtime, and varying coverage across ROS 2 distributions (Rolling down to Humble). I’ve opened an RFC on GitHub (#964 ) to discuss and define a consolidated integration test architecture before driving a broader refactor. Key Goals & Proposed Direction: Explicit Behavioral & Requirement Coverage: Shift from merely checking process/topic existence to validating physical feedback (joint position, velocity, effort command responses) for test mechanisms (slider, pendulum, gripper). Simulation Lifecycle Consolidation: Reduce redundant Gazebo/ROS 2 launches by running sequential/parallel behavioral assertions within shared simulation sessions (without sacrificing granular failure reports). Distro Harmonization: Unify semantics and implementation across Rolling , Lyrical , Kilted , Jazzy , and Humble , avoiding API lock-ins that break backports. I’ve already validated parts of this approach in [P",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-15T16:10:35+00:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-15T16:10:35+00:00",
      "source": "ROS2 Discourse",
      "section_hint": "로보틱스",
      "articleText": "[RFC] Consolidating and Modernizing Integration Test Architecture for gz_ros2_control - ros-controls Ideas - Open Robotics Discourse [RFC] Consolidating and Modernizing Integration Test Architecture for gz_ros2_control ros-controls ros-controls Ideas ros2 , ros_control , gazebo , testing Vanjoseluis October 15, 2026, 4:10pm 1 Hi everyone, Over time, the integration test suite in gz_ros2_control has grown incrementally as new controllers, demos, and interfaces were introduced. While these tests prevent regressions, the lack of a explicit test architecture currently leads to duplicate simulation launches, unnecessary CI runtime, and varying coverage across ROS 2 distributions (Rolling down to Humble). I’ve opened an RFC on GitHub (#964 ) to discuss and define a consolidated integration test architecture before driving a broader refactor. Key Goals & Proposed Direction: Explicit Behavioral & Requirement Coverage: Shift from merely checking process/topic existence to validating physical feedback (joint position, velocity, effort command responses) for test mechanisms (slider, pendulum, gripper). Simulation Lifecycle Consolidation: Reduce redundant Gazebo/ROS 2 launches by running sequential/parallel behavioral assertions within shared simulation sessions (without sacrificing granular failure reports). Distro Harmonization: Unify semantics and implementation across Rolling , Lyrical , Kilted , Jazzy , and Humble , avoiding API lock-ins that break backports. I’ve already validated parts of this approach in [PR #831 ] by redesigning the pendulum position test and introducing reusable observation utilities. Before proceeding with follow-up PRs, I’d love to gather feedback from maintainers, contributors, and the broader ROS 2 community: What specific behavioral regressions are highest priority for your workflows? Are there known edge cases in gz_ros2_control integration testing that we should address during this refactor? Feel free to share your thoughts here or join the discussion directly on the GitHub RFC issue: [RFC] Define and consolidate the integration test architecture · Issue #964 · ros-controls/gz_ros2_control · GitHub Best regards, José Luis Pérez Martín Related topics Topic Replies Views Activity Integration testing in ROS (2) Quality Assurance 2 3072 November 15, 2018 Test Framework in ROS2 ROS General ros2 3 9148 September 25, 2017 Towards a ROSdoc integation testing tutorial Quality Assurance ros2 , documentation , cmake , test 4 392 December 21, 2024 Gazebo support for ros2_control breakout session ROS General ros_control , gazebo , wg-ros2-control 2 994 January 20, 2021 New ROS online courses: GTest Framework for ROS2 Training & Education ros2 0 451 October 4, 2022",
